# issue: 601
# red_on: 185dfea3 (2026-09-16): step 3 refuses with RecoveryRequired "pending Mutation recovery operation blocks writes on branch 'main'" (the staging barrier, `staging.rs`), after the step-2 reopen succeeded; the delivery record shows the arm put stored as `__recovery/dstm-<opid>.json`
# notes: One misdirected store write, named as a store place: `storage.put` under `__recovery/*` misdirects the arm put (`recovery.rs:1154`), the same object the store-effect form of this case misdirects, so it lands as `__recovery/dstm-<opid>.json` instead of `__recovery/<opid>.json`, with a valid Armed body. The confirm put and the post-publish delete address the canonical name, so the foreign file survives the mutation.
# notes: `list_sidecars` trusts the parsed body; the heal re-reads, rewrites, and deletes the sidecar at the uri it was listed from, so the foreign-named file is healed as its operation and removed on the reopen. Before the fix (see `# red_on`) the healer deleted the canonical path rebuilt from the id, so the file was consumed by every scan and deleted by none.
# notes: Step 3 pins the write AFTER the reopen, because the claim of #601 was that the prescribed remedy (reopen) did not clear the barrier; it now does.

--- runner
timeout_ms: 10000
environments:
  - target: omnigraph-engine-dst
    storage: in-memory-object-store
    seeds: [0]

--- schema
node Person {
    name: String @key
}

--- seed
{"type":"Person","data":{"name":"alice"}}

--- seam
at: storage.put
subject: "__recovery/*"
occurrence: 1
action: misdirect
scope: next_step

--- mutate
query add_row() {
    insert Person { name: "bob" }
}

--- expect affected: nodes=1 edges=0

--- restart

--- mutate
query add_row_after_reopen() {
    insert Person { name: "carol" }
}

--- expect affected: nodes=1 edges=0
